What is Logging?

Logging is the process of recording important events, messages, warnings, and errors that occur while an application is running. It helps developers monitor application behavior, debug issues, and track execution flow.

Benefits of Logging
Helps identify errors quickly.
Simplifies debugging.
Tracks application execution.
Records important events.
Useful for monitoring production applications.
What is SLF4J?

SLF4J (Simple Logging Facade for Java) is a logging API that provides a common interface for different logging frameworks.

Advantages
Simple and lightweight.
Independent of the logging implementation.
Supports parameterized logging.
Easy to switch between logging frameworks.
What is Logback?

Logback is the default logging framework used with Spring Boot. It works together with SLF4J to generate log messages.

Features
Fast performance.
Flexible configuration.
Supports console and file logging.
Supports different log levels.
Log Levels
Level	Purpose
ERROR	Records critical errors that stop application execution.
WARN	Indicates potential problems or warnings.
INFO	Displays general application information.
DEBUG	Used for debugging during development.
TRACE	Provides detailed execution information.
1. LoggingExample.java

This program demonstrates different logging levels using SLF4J.

import org.slf4j.Logger;
import org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;

public class LoggingExample {

    private static final Logger logger =
            LoggerFactory.getLogger(LoggingExample.class);

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        logger.error("This is an error message");

        logger.warn("This is a warning message");

        logger.info("This is an information message");

        logger.debug("This is a debug message");

        logger.trace("This is a trace message");

        int userId = 42;
        String username = "Alice";

        logger.info("User logged in: id={}, username={}",
                userId, username);

        try {

            int result = 10 / 0;

        } catch (ArithmeticException e) {

            logger.error("Division by zero occurred", e);

        }

        if (logger.isDebugEnabled()) {

            logger.debug("Debug mode is enabled");

        }

    }

}
